From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netifd: expose the authoritative interface lifecycle state

The existing pending flag describes setup, not teardown. Publish native
down/setup/up/teardown state so service owners can wait for the real owner
instead of inferring teardown completion from unavailable or pending.
Keep existing up, pending and available fields unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/ubus.c
+++ b/ubus.c
@@ -826,6 +826,14 @@ netifd_dump_status(struct interface *ifa
 	struct device *dev;
 	void *a, *inactive;
 
+	static const char * const states[] = {
+		[IFS_DOWN] = "down", [IFS_SETUP] = "setup",
+		[IFS_UP] = "up", [IFS_TEARDOWN] = "teardown",
+	};
+
+	/* Pending only describes setup. Expose the authoritative protocol state
+	 * so shared-service owners can await teardown instead of inferring it. */
+	blobmsg_add_string(&b, "state", states[iface->state]);
 	blobmsg_add_u8(&b, "up", iface->state == IFS_UP);
 	blobmsg_add_u8(&b, "pending", iface->state == IFS_SETUP);
 	blobmsg_add_u8(&b, "available", iface->available);
